Well the little tricks of the trade, this was useful in a migration from 
one system to another...... Anyway, thanks "again" to Dr. Thomas P. Blinn!

Quote from his email!

"There is an implicit OSF-BASE license that should also create an implicit
two user license during installation. If you have the OSF-BASE license
registered (which you have to do AFTER you install the system), then your
implicit two user license should be loaded at boot and should work. There
is a script in /sbin/it.d/bin that creates the license; go look for it,
and when you do get logged in, use the "lmf list" and "lmf list full"
commands to verify that your licenses are registered and loading."

