Subject: DEC find vs. GNU find
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96237152125927

I seem to have stumbled over an interesting DECism with 4.0 find.  When
looking for files older than N days you can say "find . -ctime +N"  On
DEC if N is say 2 that means files created > 72 Hours ago.  if you say
"find . \( -ctime +2 -o -ctime 2 \)" I would assume you would find 
files created >72 hrs ago and 48-72 hrs ago, but you get >72 & 24-48
hrs.  To get >48 hrs N must = 1.  The GNU find and Solaris find work
the way I would expect.  Who's right? or am I just being stupid and 
that's the way it oughta be.

Jon

