X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96236757520087

Original question below.

Thanks to all those who provided help!

The trick is not use auto negotiation.  Instead explicitly
set the card to the speed you want to use.  In console mode:

	set ewa0_mode fastfd  (for 100 full duplex)

or

	set ewa0_mode fast  (for 100 half duplex)

(this can apparantly also be set using the lan_config
command but I haven't played with this)

Along with one of those that emailed help I found that
fd wasn't completely reliable (the network seemed to stall
every 10 seconds or so for a second or two).  I then tried
half duplex and all seems to be functioning well.

However.... I still have some mighty weird NFS performance
problems on the DS20, but no time this week to investigate this
further.

	- Michael


----------------------------------------------------------------------

