It's not quite a summary, but it's the solution to me.
I didn't get a usefull answer from the mailinglist already, but I found out
a few things:

Mirroring rz8/rz9
rz9 doesn't have to be in rootdg already
Common is to mirror the OS disk before the encapsulate of the OS-disk

I had to write the original disklabel of the OS-disk rz8 (from _before_ the
encapsulate) to rz9.
The original label was in
/etc/vol/reconfig.d/disk.d/rz8e.encapdone/disklabel.orig
Eerst rz9 uit lsm-config halen:

# voldisk rm rz9 (disk was already in use by lsm, so I had to get it out)
# disklabel -R -r rz9
/etc/vol/reconfig.d/disk.d/rz8e.encapdone/disklabel.orig xxx

Next step is to put all partitions on the rz9 disklabel to 'unused'
# disklabel -r rz9
# disklabel -Fs /dev/rrz9x -where x represents the partitions: execute this
command for a,b and g, and maybe any other AdvFs partition in use

Mirroring will now succeed:
# volrootmir -a rz9
 Mirroring rootvol to rz9a.
  Mirroring swapvol to rz9b.
  Mirroring vol-rz8d to rz9d.
  Mirroring vol-rz8g to rz9g.

I still have a question left:
How to setup/change the (alpha)console variables so that the default
boot_dev is rz8, but when it's not there the OS should boot from rz9??

Any suggestions?
