Hello all,

the question to distribute the printcap via NIS leaded to
no direct solution as long the OS lpd is used.

As Werner Rost suggests one should run a set of rsh scripts
to automate the princap modifications on remote machines
because there should be separate error and spool file/directory
locations for each printer. Of course this is NOT a real problem
at all!;  but I tried to direct these files to automount points
and the lpd seems to take care of that even with ".nfs*" files
for file locking - but lpd doesn't look at a NIS map and
accessing automount points "odds" one more dependency you must
take care for while entering run level 3.

Many thanks to you all

Uwe


