1) About the lsof part : 
   -------------------

Thanks to Vic Abell (the lsof author himself) who says :

This is an internal lsof problem that is probably caused by a
mismatch between the version of DEC OSF/1, DU, or Tru64 UNIX for
which lsof was built and the one on the system on which lsof is
being run.  It could possibly be an lsof bug, but none like it has
ever been reported to me.

I suggest you start by getting the lsof source distribution from:

        ftp://vic.cc.purdue.edu/pub/tools/unix/lsof

and build lsof for yourself on the system where you want to run
it.  If the "no file * space" error persists, send me some e-mail
and we'll see if we can figure out what is happening.

+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

2) About /usr/share/sysman/bin/insightd part :
   -----------------------------------------
Thanks to Dr. Tom Blinn who explained :

When in doubt, use "grep" on the *.inv files in /usr/.smdb. to see if
the daemon was delivered as part of the standard system software (it
was),  and use "grep" to look at the startup scripts in /sbin/init.d
to see how it gets started (that is, what component seems to depend on
it).

I can't say why there are no reference pages.  There probably should be.
If this is a problem for you, you might want to file a formal problem
report with Compaq Services.

Oh, yes,  it's the Compaq Insight Manager, used for network based (web)
system management.  If there is documentation, it's probably somewhere
in the system management guide book.

