My original question:

> > We have a test cluster running 5.0a with a 4100 and a 2100 in it.
> >
> > We are seeing severe packet loss on the 2100 (running 10 megabit half
> > duplex on the interface on the combo card) and are trying to track down
> > the problem. The cluster has been acting strangely which may be a by
> > product of the packet loss.
> >
> > We are uncomfortable with gated, which is required for the cluster.
> > Does anyone have a gated.conf file from a 5.0a cluster that they could
> > share with us for a comparison??
> >

The answer:

We have DECNET running to provide the rfc1006 (tcp to osi) capability 
necessary to run the Compaq X.500/LDAP server.

Turns out that DECNET is not yet setup to understand clusters, so 
although I configured DECNET for a single cluster node, when other 
machines in the cluster were rebooted DECNET would start up on those 
machines with a conflicting MAC address which caused all kinds of grief.

We were able to make DECNET cluster safe by creating CDSL directories 
for /var/dna and /var/dss and configuring each machine individually 
with decnetsetup.

So, although 5.0a clusters are now supported, not all applications are 
clustersafe out of the box.


