From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Jun 15 20:09:31 2000
From: Sylvain Robitaille <syl () alcor ! concordia ! ca>
Date: Thu, 15 Jun 2000 20:09:31 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: DS-10 with a serial terminal for console: Booting from CD
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96109982800816


As usual, this mailing list provides prompt responses with quality
information.

Earlier I wrote:

> I'm trying to install an OS (DU-4.0e) on a DS-10 we recently purchased
> (standard practice here -- we have yet to use a factory-intsalled OS),
> but I can't seem to get the system booted from the CD.

I hope the respondants won't mind, but I'm not going to list them all
here. There were simply too many, (and probably more arriving as I type
this summary).

Some great suggestions were made that may be useful to others.
Generally, it seems I was doing everything right...

- Make sure to use the correct serial port (serial port "1" on all the
  systems we have, but I wouldn't be surprised if there were some
  systems where that isn't the case). If you type 'init' at the SRM
  prompt the self-test messages only go to the "right" serial port.

- Make sure the environment variables are set correctly:

    console    serial
    os_type    unix

- make sure the firmware is current. Newer versions of the OS often
  require firmware upgrades.

The problem, in my case, however is simply that the DS10 is not
supported by version 4.0e of the OS. I managed to get confirmation from
two of the folks at Compaq that the DS10 requires at least
Tru64-Unix-4.0F.

Thanks to all those who replied.

