Subject: How to set inital file ownership
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96108784310155

Hi managers,

we have a Tru64-Unix 4.0F cluster running with NIS, enhanced security and
file quotas enabled.

For several projects we have created specific NIS-groups and NIS-users and
given the specific NIS-group as secondary group membership to those users
who work on these projects. Each project has got its own directory tree.

By doing this, each member of a project has access to the project
directory, but each file he creates there sets this users as file owner.
This however means that each file, though created in the project
directory, is added to his private file quota, which is no good, it should
be added to the projects file quota.

So what we need is:
- each user has got his private file quota inside his primary group
- each project has got its specific project file quota
- project members have access to the project's directory though it's not
  their primary NIS group
- files created in the project's directory should have project owner and 
  project group as default owner and default group, file size has to be
  added to the projects file quota. 

By setting the set-group-ID bit with  chmod g+rwxs  to the directory we
can set the default group ownership. But how to set the default file ownership
equal to the ownership of the directory?

Thanks for your suggestions and help - Axel

