Greetings Managers:

I received many replies regarding the max number of disks and initialization
time of a 20x9GB RAID5 raidset.
Most concurred that the max number of disks is 14 for the HSZ70 controller,
which makes the possibility of creating this set slim. A couple believed
that 20 is possible.
I received estimates of a couple hours to more than twelve, so the downtime
is definitely a factor.

