member.  We fixed this and recreated the stripe set.  This is now visible to
DUNIX.

My recovery procedures are basically:

1.  voldisk rm xxx
2.  write a new label to the fixed disk.
3.  voldisksetup -i xxx nconfig=2 nlog=2 privlen=1024
4. voldg -g ddd -k adddisk xxx=xxx
5. volrecover -g sss -sb

And I am quite comfortable with this.  However, as the physical disk has
multiple sub-disks, do I need to manually recreate the individual sub disks
(between steps 4 & 5 above) before recovering the disk group - or will LSM
be cleaver enough to do this itself.

This is a production machine so I don't want to get it wrong!!

Any help is appreciated.

Tony

