Summary:

Thanks to Chang Song <song@zk3.dec.com> who analyzed our crash dumps
and quickly provided a fixed version of /sys/BINARY/ufs.mod . A new
kernel built with this module runs fine, and rvdump completed dumping
the UFS partition in question for the first time since we switched
to V5.0 .

I assume an official patch is likely to be released soon through
the usual channels.

Original posting:

> we are running OSF/1 V5.0 on an AlphaStation 600A and the system 
> reproducably crashes with a kernel memory fault while running rvdump
> on a UFS partiotion of 4 GB size and 74% usage. The crash data
> appended below indicate there is a problem in the code related
> to ufs_ioctl() which leads to a memory fault in ufs_get_extentmap().
> The kernel patches from patchkit 2 have already been applied, but
> there seems to be no patch yet for this problem.

