Hi all,

I was inquiring whether anyone had managed to get the IMAP daemon supplied
with v5.0 up and running under C2.

Thanks to Nikola Milutinovic and Richard Rogers for their responses.  
They had both managed to get Cyrus's version of the IMAP daemon (which is
what the one supplied with v5.0 is based on) working with C2 by compiling
it themselves, although they hadn't tried the one supplied with the OS.  
In the end I used the University of Washington's IMAP daemon which suits
our needs better and works well.  

So I still don't know whether I was doing something wrong in the setup or
if the daemon really isn't built to cope with C2.  My feeling is that the
IMAP daemon was somewhat rushed into the release of v5.0, (particularly
seeing as it isn't even installed with the correct permissions, and the
version supplied is 1.5.2 rather the 1.6.x which is the current stream)
and that to run it, you need to be at Base security.  Hopefully someone
can prove me wrong...

