before the machine starts swapping?

^^^ original message ^^^

The most relevant reply came from Nick Hill:

>From the information you provided the physical memory is being fully
used. Top reports 1040K free memory and vmstat is showing little free
memory, between 68 and 126 free pages which are both less than 1M byte
of free memory. Other processes must be taking memory of the buffer
cache and/or Advfs cache may be using it if there is heavy I/O going on.
vmstat -P will show how many pages are in the ubc.

A similar reply came from Tim Tahaney:

Buy some more memory, vmstat shows 488k in use, thats 8k*488k=3.84gb in
use.

Other suggestions included:

- run syscheck: I did, but didn't have the time yet to implement the
  changes it recommended

- check limits (memory, vmemory) for the users running each process:
  not a problem in my case

