Content-type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Content-transfer-encoding: 7bit

Hi All,

We are running DU4.0F on an AlphaServer.  I have installed tcpwrappers,
and use /etc/hosts.allow and /etc/hosts.deny to limit access to most
daemons to just a few well-known hosts.  This works very well.  Most of
the time, we use ssh whenever we have to access this machine remotely.

However, we occasionally attend conferences where there is only telnet
access.  We just want to be able to log in and check email, typically,
use pine or some text-based mailer.  So, what I have done is create a
single dummy account, with limited priveleges.   All of our group
members know the password to this account.  The idea is then if a person
is at a conference somewhere and can only use telnet, they can log into
the AlphaServer using the dummy account, and then ssh from there to
their own account.

What I want to know is, how do I set it up so that one cannot telnet
into any account except this special dummy account?

Cheers,
Ed.

--Boundary_(ID_sxAb80K5xHN8tjeKePmlSw)
