From tru64-unix-managers  Sun Jun 11 20:33:55 2000
From: cstaub - Craig Stauber <cstaub () acxiom ! com>
Date: Sun, 11 Jun 2000 20:33:55 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Will Tru64 run on DEC Alpha 500a?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96086825814636

Thank you for the great answers.  Here's the summary and some clips of the
answers.  

Question: 
 We are considering the purchase of a DEC 500a with the following
attributes.
 
 500Mhz 21164 Alpha based System
 DEC Alpha 500a 128MB RAM
 4GB SCSI-II FW hard drive
 12X IDE CDROM
 4Mb Matrox PCI video card
 10/100mbts ethernet card & sound built in
 OS-Linux 6.2 installed.
 Since this machine is not an "AU" and it is currently running Linux, is
 there a firmware upgrade that will allow this machine to be converted to
SRM
 so we can install Tru64 Unix?  I seem to remember Compaq issued firmware
 upgrades for these machines after AlphaNT sundown was announced.

Answers:

"I had to upgrade the firmware AND swap out all the video cards. I don't
recall what card I replaced, but had to put in an ATI Mach 64 card instead
(widely available). I don't think the Matrox card is supported by
Tru64UNIX."

"The firmware is not the problem.  There is an option in the BIOS to select
SRM console.  It should already be loaded, although you'll probably want to
update to the latest version.  The problem might be the options in the
system.  There were some issues between the A and the AU versions as to what
graphics and SCSI cards were supported. I think when we did the conversion,
we had to order a different graphics card,"

"You will however need a different graphics card as the Matrox cards are not
supported in UNIX."

"Yes these will run Tru64. The "A" means it can only hold one console at a
time (SRM or AlphaBios). The
only problem I see with your configuration is the Matrox card. It is not
supported in graphics mode
(CDE) but will run in text mode fine.  The latest firmware update is version
5.7."

"Matrox graphics cards are not supported by Tru64.  You'll need to get one
that is, unless you're willing to use the serial console port to get the
system up and do everything graphical remotely using X."

"This card is not supported under Tru64 UNIX. You'd have to get another
display adapter, if you need any kind of graphics. Of course, you _can_
install without graphics capability, though."
 

My thanks to all who responded!

